Master: any
# Expect: waiting
# LateAfter (park) demo (specs 0030/0024): a clone proto whose clones are created but held back for an
# operator. LateAfter (park) (00:00) is earlier than StartAfter (00:01), so both deadlines are behind us
# the moment a clone exists — and a job initialized at or after its LateAfter (park) is parked on entry
# instead of being dispatched: each clone lands in `manual` (event `park_after`) and nothing runs
# by itself.
#
# Unpark a clone to run it (borg unpark demo/clones/manual_books~book1, or the UI button); it runs
# at once, since StartAfter has passed. Unparking after the LateAfter (park) deadline sticks — the clone
# is not re-parked. Do the clones one by one, in any order; demo/clones/manual_summary waits for
# all of them. (A `rerun`/`clean` of a clone parks it again, being past the deadline.)
#
# On a clone proto these deadlines are its clones' only (spec 0121): the proto itself is never
# parked, and only waits on its clones.
Type: clone
CloneListSource: PROC<demo/clones/gen_books>
LateAfter: 00:00 park
StartAfter: 00:01
Command: echo "manually released: %<book> (tag %<clone>)"
Host: any
